  The endjin blog carrying every syndication extension this library reads from an RSS feed. No real feed
  looks like this and none should; the file exists so that one load exercises every RSS-side extension
  adapter, which is why the same post carries geocoding, trackback and podcast metadata at once.

  Two corrections against the file this replaced, both found by fingerprinting what actually attached
  rather than by reading the markup:

    * cf: was declared and never used, so SimpleListSyndicationExtension never attached and its example
      printed nothing but "Loaded" and "Saved". It now carries a real cf:treatAs and cf:listinfo.
    * sx: was bound to http://www.microsoft.com/schemas/rss/core/2005, the Simple List namespace.
      FeedSync's namespace is http://feedsync.org/2007/feedsync. The extension attached anyway, on the
      strength of the prefix, which is exactly the sort of accident a corpus should not be teaching.
-->
